  "details": "Strange crash that happens under specific circumstances. It seems so niche a problem, that I am not sure how important this is. I first noticed this since the 1446 build (April 2023). The steps to repeat are as follows:\n\n1. Open VRChat on PC (either Desktop or VR mode)\n\n2. Load into a world/instance. \n\n3. Outside of VRC, move VRC game window below taskbar so that it is hidden beneath the bottom edge of the monitor screen. Also note, that the VRChat Window must be the selected, \"on-top\" window for the crash to occur (after moving the window to beneath the taskbar, simply click the top of the VRC window to ensure it is \"selected\").\n\n4. Without deselecting the VRChat window, wait about 10 minutes; the previous 3 steps must be complete within 10 minutes of the game starting, or the crash will not occur. \n\n5. After a few minutes, VRChat should crash.\n\nI have included a video recording of the process, from setting up the steps outline above, to the actual crash itself (Sorry for the poor quality; it was hard fitting a 7 minute video under 8mb). \n\nIf you need more information, please let me know.",
